<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gov't says happy with CVRD premium.</title>
<headline>Brazil gov't says happy with CVRD premium.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian Planning Minister Antonio Kandir said he was happy with the 3.337 billion reais paid for a controlling stake in mining giant Companhia Vale do Rio Doce (CVRD) and the 19.98 percent premium paid.</p>
<p>&quot;The premium was above expectations,&quot; Kandir told reporters in the Rio de Janeiro bolsa where 41.7 percent of CVRD voting stock was sold to the Valepar consortium led by Brazilian steelmaker CSN for 32 reais a share.</p>
</text>
